# GD-4 (round 19, writer 10): L §8.3 item 10: buy, a random movement, books konto, so bal(konto, …) on an ask line
# without a query is refused at load (LOAD-RANDOM `<line> is random; apply a query`), no longer at the read. The old
# comment:
# E §3.1 step 10: "An ask line whose value is random that neither applies a query nor replays a path ... [is]
# refused (LOAD-RANDOM, LANGUAGE §5.16)"; L §8.3 `<line> is random; apply a query`. konto's balance after the 15th
# reaches spend[2026-01] through buy's amount. refcore's load marks the random cone over inputs and defs only, so it
# finds this at the read and stops the reality as a load refusal does (errors.RandomLine).
=== m.tally
model r
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source own "own"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind spends: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2020-01-01..
place shop: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input spend_mu: money PLN
input spend_sd: money PLN
input spend_dom: int
def spend[m in months]: dist PLN = normal(spend_mu, spend_sd) to 1e-9 at end_of(m)

move buy[m in months]: spends
  on day_of(m, spend_dom)
  at end_of(m)
  leg cash from konto to shop amount round(spend[m], minor(PLN), half-even)

version v
  cite own
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  spend_mu = 1 000.00 PLN "own"
  spend_sd = 100.00 PLN "own"
  spend_dom = 15 "own"
  opening[konto] = 10 000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "statement"

ask r1: bal(konto, 2026-03-31)
=== expect
refused: LOAD-RANDOM ask r1: bal(konto, 2026-03-31) is random; apply a query (m.tally:32)
